{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "units": "mm",
  "meta": {
    "title": "Book-Fold Phone",
    "notes": "Graph twin of main.py. Same components, same order, same operations, so the two engines' bounding boxes and volumes agree exactly. COMPOSITION: node ids carry the component slug as a prefix (framehalf_, foldabledisplay_, displaypanel_, hingefold_, lenswindow_, systembuttons_, port_, cardslot_, speaker_) so a reader can see where one hyperobject ends and the next begins; the assembly's own chain is prefixed asm_. The literal spelling `component:<slug>` is not available — the transpiler's node-id grammar is ^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*$, so a colon fails validation before the graph ever renders. Sub-graph reuse (yantra4d lane G-CLUSTERS) is what would let this twin REFERENCE a component cartridge rather than inline its nodes; until it lands the nodes are duplicated here. GEOMETRY NOTE: the fold axis IS the X axis through the origin, in the MIDDLE OF THE GAP between the two half-frames, which is why the fold is one `rotate` about x with no compensating translate (`rotate` turns about the origin and nothing else) and why the gap vanishes when the device opens — a turn about that axis lands the camera half in the cover half's own z band. The crease relief is a cylinder ON that axis, so it is invariant under the fold and can be cut before the rotate. NO EXPRESSIONS (lane G-EXPR): every derived dimension is its own parameter — hingefold_leaf_cyl.r is the relief radius less the archetype's 0.3 mm running clearance, and every *_center_* value places a solid the engine cannot compute. Worse here than in the clamshell: the HINGE GAP, the one dimension that defines this family, cannot be a control at all, because the only things that carry it are the two halves' frozen centre-Z constants. Telesia's scripts/device-presets.py emits them together from one registry entry, so they cannot drift. TWO THINGS THIS TWIN CANNOT SAY and main.py can: a port or card tray that is absent on a device (no branching — the twin always cuts both), and a feature count of zero (pattern counts clamp to 1).",
    "frame": "X = hinge_axis_length, the long axis, and the fold axis through the origin. Y = the folding axis: the cover half runs from y=0 to +cover_half_width, the camera half the same and then turns. Z: the gap mid-plane is z=0; closed depth is 2 x half_thickness + the gap, open depth is half_thickness."
  },
  "nodes": [
